Bluetooth: no duplicates filter while an LE connection is pending

The kernel makes a pending LE connection from an advertising report of the
peer (check_pending_le_conn).  The Pro1X's WCN3990 keeps its duplicates
filter across a scan restart: it reported the peer (a Tesla's VCSEC) once,
then never during the 25 s of each connection attempt while other devices
kept being reported, and no LE Create Connection was ever sent (btmon,
2026-11-19, 7 attempts).  Scan without the duplicates filter while a
connection is pending, in passive scanning and in discovery.

Not upstream; the pro1x channel's.
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -3258,6 +3258,14 @@
 	} else if (hci_is_le_conn_scanning(hdev)) {
 		window = hdev->le_scan_window_connect;
 		interval = hdev->le_scan_int_connect;
+
+		/* A pending connection is made from an advertising report of
+		 * the peer.  Controllers whose duplicates filter outlives a
+		 * scan restart (WCN3990) report the peer once and never again,
+		 * so the connection never starts: no duplicates filter while
+		 * one is pending.
+		 */
+		filter_dups = LE_SCAN_FILTER_DUP_DISABLE;
 	} else if (hci_is_adv_monitoring(hdev)) {
 		window = hdev->le_scan_window_adv_monitor;
 		interval = hdev->le_scan_int_adv_monitor;
@@ -6304,7 +6312,10 @@
 	if (err < 0)
 		own_addr_type = ADDR_LE_DEV_PUBLIC;
 
-	if (hci_is_adv_monitoring(hdev) ||
+	/* As for passive scanning: a pending LE connection needs every
+	 * report of its peer.
+	 */
+	if (hci_is_adv_monitoring(hdev) || hci_is_le_conn_scanning(hdev) ||
 	    (hci_test_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_STRICT_DUPLICATE_FILTER) &&
 	    hdev->discovery.result_filtering)) {
 		/* Duplicate filter should be disabled when some advertisement
